{"id":"20260829T004340.061276360Z-4023a231","time":"2026-08-29T00:43:40.06127636Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW7VbuTbYbxj9ChKYa5F\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Implemented the bounded plan; nothing beyond it.\\n\\n**What changed** (4 files, +258, no deletions, no signature changes, no new files):\\n\\n1. `internal/workflow/testedit.go:238` — `confineToPlannedFiles(diff string, planned []string) error`, beside `inspectTestEdits`/`diffFileStates`. Reads paths through `report.FromDiff(diff).Files` (every status; both sides of a rename), canonicalises the named set with `path.Clean(strings.TrimSpace(f))` exactly as `architecturalFiles` does, and returns an error naming every path outside the plan and the plan's named files. It takes the diff and the named files only — no grant input, so no grant can enlarge the set. A small `plannedOrNone` helper keeps a plan that named nothing from rendering as blank.\\n\\n2. `internal/workflow/engine.go:1250` — called in `runCandidate` immediately after the `ModeInspect` refusal and before the `candidate.changed` event, returning `(false, plan, lastReview, lastAudit, err)` the way that refusal does. Validation, audit, Level-1 classification, review and admission are all downstream of it; the worktree is untouched.\\n\\n3. `internal/workflow/engine_test.go` — `TestCandidateWiderThanPlanIsRefusedBeforeReview` (unnamed path refused by name, named-only diff passes including the plan's `./` spelling, deletion outside the plan refused, rename out of the plan refused, plus source-order assertions that the check sits after the read-only refusal and before the event/validate/audit/classify), `TestOperationalTestGrantDoesNotExpandPlanScope` (real grant fixture from `testedit_test.go`, grantable-but-unn