{"id":"20260829T005015.006581183Z-ebe27e27","time":"2026-08-29T00:50:15.006581183Z","session_id":"session-20260829T003802.236153648Z","task_id":"task-1787963882236621025","source":"claude","kind":"output","summary":"{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CeW7zywLGCtNRZXuGf6BU\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Cycle-2 review finding [f1] is reconciled.\\n\\n## What the finding was right about\\n\\n`e.validate` runs mutating formatters **first**, then calls `CandidateDiff` and returns the re-read diff (`internal/workflow/engine.go:4400-4410`). A formatter is a configured command with write access to the whole worktree, and `CandidateCapture` does `git add --intent-to-add .`, so a file a formatter creates lands in the returned diff. The single pre-validation check therefore bounded the worker's bytes, not the bytes the audit, Level-1 classification, reviewer and admission actually consume.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/engine.go`** — the pre-validation check is kept, and the same check is applied again to the diff `e.validate` returns, immediately after it returns and before `event.ValidationRun` is emitted (so before `inspectProspectiveSurfaces`, `inspectTestEdits`, `awareness_audit_diff`, `classifyForDarkRun` and `reviewPacket` see it). Same refusal shape, same return.\\n\\nBoth checks are retained deliberately: the pre-validation one attributes a widening to the worker, which a post-validation-only check would attribute to the formatter.\\n\\n**`internal/workflow/engine_test.go`** — `TestAFormatterCannotWidenTheCandidateAfterValidation`, behavioral rather than structural: real temp git repo, a worker edit confined to `planned.go` that the first check passes, then `e.validate` with `Validation.Format` set to a command that writes `generated.go`. It asserts the formatter really did widen the re-read diff (otherwise the test says so and fails rather than passing vacuously), that the validation bundle itself is content with it, and that the returned diff is refused by name. The ordering assertion then pins that the second call precedes every downstream consumer.\\n\\nMutation-checked: with the new call removed, the test fails with *\\\"the diff validation returns is never confined; only the worker's own diff is\\\"*.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\n- `gofmt -l cmd internal` — clean\\n- `go vet ./...` — clean\\n- `go test ./...` — all packages pass\\n\\nSensei preflight on the changed files: `PREFLIGHT_STATUS_OK`, authoritative, `CONFIDENCE_HIGH`, coverage sufficient (6 anchors / 2 files), blast radius local, approval gate none, no forbidden fixes. `invariant:sensei_code.workflow.context_never_widens_worker_scope` is the directly relevant critical invariant and this change strengthens rather than relaxes it.\\n\\n## Scope note\\n\\nI implemented only [f1]. The plan's four named files are unchanged as a set; my cycle-2 diff touches `internal/workflow/engine.go` and `internal/workflow/engine_test.go`, both named — this candidate is itself confined to its plan.\\n\\nOne thing I did not do, because the plan does not contain it: the review asked to \\\"prove no audit or review is reached,\\\" and there is no test harness in this repo that can drive `runCandidate` end to end (it needs a live `sensei.Client`, an installed capability guard and a real worker process; no fake exists). I proved the behavioral half for real — a real formatter really widening a real re-read diff, really refused — and pinned the \\\"nothing downstream sees it\\\" half by source ordering against six named downstream call sites. Building a `runCandidate` test harness would be a larger change than the plan authorises; flagging it for the architect rather than deciding it.\\n\\nAWG: briefing(internal/workflow/engine.go) | invariants: context_never_widens_worker_scope, repeated_resume_cannot_mint_authority | uncertainty: no end-to-end runCandidate harness exists, so \\\"no audit or review is reached\\\" is proven behaviorally at the validate boundary and structurally past it\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":966,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":79994,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":966},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3b770486-84cf-43d5-b3c2-459abc75ede2\",\"uuid\":\"46aea2ee-8d91-4c96-96bb-452859c5d0cd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-08-29T00:50:15.005Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CeW7zy6yM1sDP9uaRLnn3\"}","payload":{"stream":"stdout"}}
